TouchRDP PERF-9: per-thread opt-out of hardware (VideoToolbox) H.264 decoding.

Upstream FreeRDP uses hardware decoding unconditionally once compiled in. Since
3.32.0 that is FFmpeg's generic WITH_FFMPEG_HWACCEL path (WITH_VIDEOTOOLBOX is a
deprecated alias that turns it on; on macOS the device type is VideoToolbox). Each
GFX surface's H264_CONTEXT is created lazily inside the SurfaceCommand handler,
with no way to pass a per-session preference through the H264 API. This adds a
thread-local flag plus an exported setter; the client wraps
RdpgfxClientContext::SurfaceCommand and sets the flag immediately before
delegating (same thread, same call), so each session's decoder inherits its own
choice. With the flag off, the decoder is opened with useHwDecoder = FALSE (pure
software). Default (1) is upstream behaviour. Applied by Tools/build-freerdp.sh;
Sources/CRDPBridge/rdpbridge.c dlsym()s the setter so an unpatched library still
links and simply ignores the toggle. Ported to 3.32.1 (was against 3.31.1).

--- a/libfreerdp/codec/h264_ffmpeg.c
+++ b/libfreerdp/codec/h264_ffmpeg.c
@@ -40,6 +40,22 @@
     but your version of libavutil is too old !Disabling.
 #undef WITH_FFMPEG_HWACCEL
 #endif
+#endif
+
+#ifdef WITH_FFMPEG_HWACCEL
+/* TouchRDP (Tools/freerdp-patches): per-thread opt-out of hardware H.264 decoding.
+ * Upstream decodes on the hardware unconditionally once compiled in. The H264_CONTEXT
+ * is created lazily inside the GFX surface-command handler, so a client that wraps
+ * RdpgfxClientContext::SurfaceCommand can set this immediately before delegating —
+ * same thread, same call — and each session's decoder inherits its own preference
+ * without any change to the H264 API. Default 1 == upstream behaviour. */
+static _Thread_local int s_videotoolbox_preferred = 1;
+
+FREERDP_API void freerdp_h264_set_thread_videotoolbox_preference(int enabled);
+void freerdp_h264_set_thread_videotoolbox_preference(int enabled)
+{
+	s_videotoolbox_preferred = enabled ? 1 : 0;
+}
 #endif
 
 /* Fallback support for older libavcodec versions */
@@ -1377,6 +1393,12 @@
 #endif
 
 #ifdef WITH_FFMPEG_HWACCEL
+		if (!sys->hwctx && sys->useHwDecoder && !s_videotoolbox_preferred)
+		{
+			WLog_Print(h264->log, WLOG_INFO,
+			           "Hardware H264 decoding disabled for this session, using software");
+			sys->useHwDecoder = FALSE;
+		}
 		if (sys->useHwDecoder && (sys->type != AV_HWDEVICE_TYPE_NONE))
 			WLog_Print(h264->log, WLOG_DEBUG,
 			           "Trying to initialize hardware backed decoder of type %s",
